The Towers of Hanoi	These two programs are based upon the one in the book_The_Age_of_Intelligent_Machines by Raymond Kurzweil.  (ISBN 0-262-11121-7)	They solve the famous towers of hanoi problem recursively.The hanoi program gives instructions on how to solve the problem, andthe hanoimod program shows the answer.For example:$ hanoi 3Move disk 1 from tower 1 to tower 2Move disk 2 from tower 1 to tower 3Move disk 1 from tower 2 to tower 3Move disk 3 from tower 1 to tower 2Move disk 1 from tower 3 to tower 1Move disk 2 from tower 3 to tower 2Move disk 1 from tower 1 to tower 2$ hanoimod 31	3 22	131	32	13	21	323	2 112	33	2 11	12	33	21	12	3 2312	3 2 13	Beware, this program grows exponentially.  hanoi n creates  n(2  - 1) lines.  (E. g. hanoi 20 creates 1,048,575 lines.)(I compiled this on a System V/386 Release 3.2 UNIX.  I see no reasonwhy it shouldn't work on other systems, but I haven't tested it.)  